{"id":"changes-timeline","label":"Figure 7","title":"What changed, December 2024 to October 2026, by status","kind":"chart","synthesis":"data","refs":[1,2,3,5,7,24,25,27,28,29,35,59,61,140,142,143,227,228,233,276,291,292,312,313,314,317,318,319,321,322,323,325,340,374,377,380,382,386,389,391,392,400,401,402,403,404,405,406,407,408,409,410,417,418,436,484,486,487,488,489,490,502,503,504,509,510,513,519,521,522,546,547,548,549,575,584,622,623,625,627,630,631,697,699,700,701,704,720,721,723,724,728,765,806,828,829,1032,1033,1036,1040,1046,1047,1048,1108,1110,1129,1238,1241,1242,1252,1255,1262,1263,1264,1265,1266,1267,1269,1270,1272,1273,1274,1277,1278,1279,1280,1288,1295,1303,1311,1325,1344,1398,1401,1405,1406,1421],"data":"figures/data/changes-timeline.csv","script":"figures/scripts/changes-timeline.py","chart":{"type":"scatter","x":{"field":"plot_date","label":"Date of the change","unit":"date"},"y":{"field":"status","label":"Status"},"series":{"field":"basis","label":"How the change is sourced"}},"caption":"The 51 dated changes recorded between December 2024 and October 2026, placed by date and by status: final, class deviation, pending implementation, proposed or announced. The series says how each is sourced. Most of the anchors of this guide moved inside the window: the order for the FAR overhaul (April 15, 2025) [386](#cite:386), the threshold rise (October 1, 2025) [417](#cite:417), the fiscal year 2026 defense authorization act (December 18, 2025) [1273](#cite:1273) [1033](#cite:1033), the SBIR and STTR reauthorization (April 13, 2026) [1](#cite:1), the CMMC Phase II suspension (announced July 13, 2026) [625](#cite:625) and the 8(a) rule (final August 11, 2026, effective September 10, 2026) [314](#cite:314). Eight items are known here only from secondary sources or from texts that could not be read, and they are marked as such. Left off the chart: one record dated only to the year 2025, NSF Translation to Practice [1401](#cite:1401), and three records dated outside the window.","how_to_read":"Time runs left to right and each row is a status, so you can see at a glance what is law (final), what is in use by deviation, what is enacted but not yet implemented, and what is only proposed or announced. Each point is one change record; points stacked at one date happened on the same day. Check the series before you rely on a point: anything not marked as read from a primary text is reported, not confirmed. A point shows when a change was made or announced, which is not always when it takes effect.","explain":[{"on":"y: status","text":"The status word on the change record. Final means a law, final rule or completed action; class-deviation means agencies follow new text while the codified text stays in force; pending-implementation means enacted with no implementing document found; proposed and announced carry no legal effect yet."},{"on":"series: basis","text":"How the record is sourced: primary (the governing text or official page was read), primary-partial (read in part), secondary-only (reported by commentary only), unread (the text is listed but could not be read) or unconfirmed (not confirmed as live)."},{"on":"points at 2025-12-18","text":"Ten records share December 18, 2025: nine on the fiscal year 2026 defense authorization act and one on DoD class deviations dated the same day. Sections 1802, 1823 and 1804 were verified in the U.S. Code [1273](#cite:1273) [1033](#cite:1033) [1036](#cite:1036); sections 1822, 1824 and 824 were read as headings only and their content comes from digests [806](#cite:806) [1108](#cite:1108)."},{"on":"plot_date","text":"The date field of the record. Three records give only a month and are placed on its first day; the date_precision column marks them."},{"on":"class-deviation row","text":"The FAR overhaul reaches contracts this way for now: model text is issued part by part and adopted agency by agency. Part 19 was taken up by GSA from November 3, 2025 and by DoD from February 1, 2026 [400](#cite:400) [402](#cite:402)."}],"hotspots":[],"concepts":["where-the-numbers-live","how-a-buy-happens"],"discussed_in":["8-what-changed","1-why-this-matters","9-how-to-read"],"source":"One row per record in changes.yaml dated from December 2024 to October 2026; date, status, basis and sources are copied from the record and the short title is the builder's. Month-only dates are plotted on the first of the month (plot_date) with the original kept in date. Nothing else was converted.","table":{"rows":[{"id":"chg-collaboration-guidelines-withdrawn","date":"2024-12-11","plot_date":"2024-12-11","date_precision":"day","status":"final","basis":"primary","title":"FTC and DOJ withdraw competitor-collaboration guidelines","affects":"teaming-contractor-team-arrangements;joint-venture-set-aside","ref":"765;828;829"},{"id":"chg-dfars-sbir-data-rights","date":"2025-01-17","plot_date":"2025-01-17","date_precision":"day","status":"final","basis":"primary","title":"DFARS SBIR data rights: single 20-year period","affects":"data-rights-marking;data-rights-as-a-subcontractor;sbir-sttr-phase-iii;phase-iii-award","ref":"24;25;228;233"},{"id":"chg-sdb-goal-reset","date":"2025-02-24","plot_date":"2025-02-24","date_precision":"day","status":"announced","basis":"primary","title":"SBA returns the SDB goal to 5%","affects":"sdb-self-representation;8a-business-development","ref":"317;374;377;380"},{"id":"chg-software-memo-2025-03","date":"2025-03-06","plot_date":"2025-03-06","date_precision":"day","status":"final","basis":"primary-partial","title":"Software acquisition memo: CSOs and OTs the default","affects":"aaf-software-acquisition;diu-cso","ref":"1252;1255;1264"},{"id":"chg-fsrs-retired","date":"2025-03-08","plot_date":"2025-03-08","date_precision":"day","status":"final","basis":"primary","title":"FSRS.gov retired; subaward reporting moves to SAM.gov","affects":"ffata-subaward-reporting;finding-subcontract-work","ref":"697;723;724;728"},{"id":"chg-eo-14240-gsa-consolidation","date":"2025-03-2